lient 1.4.0. Single HTML with pinned CDN libraries.\\\",\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Procedural low-poly mansion diorama, cel-shaded teal and plum surfaces, ink outlines, parchment and amber matchlight\\\",\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Three.js AnimationMixer and authored AnimationClip / NumberKeyframeTrack animations for explorers, ghosts, bats, spiders and clocks; procedural particles and camera drift\\\",\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Original code-synthesized chamber-style music (10% default), synthesized sound effects and Animalese-style gibberish voices; no audio files\\\",\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"1–4 player shared-world co-op through AI Hub; standalone same-browser rooms using BroadcastChannel and cross-device WebRTC invitation/reply codes\\\",\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless simulation and scripted full playthrough, Chromium WebGPU, virtual standard gamepad, touch device profiles, Web Audio analyser, two-page co-op, AI Hub conformance harness; visual screenshots for composition. Physical controller and real mobile hardware: unknown.\\\",\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"none; native model knowledge only. Supplied AI Hub integration files read and pinned dependencies downloaded.\\\",\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Codex CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max\\\",\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\n  },\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"],\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"Three.js TSL makes it straightforward to give every generated object consistent stepped lighting and ink edges.\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"The room topology, authoritative cooperative simulation, controller-focused menus, procedural art and synthesized audio.\\\", \\\"Coordinating WebGPU initialization, fixed-step Rapier movement, native animation and snapshots while keeping a single-file deliverable.\\\", \\\"none\\\", \\\"A first-party controller navigation and accessibility layer for game menus would save substantial integration work.\\\"],\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"The source, controller-first direction and complete-demo requirements gave the game a clear identity.\\\", \\\"The request to avoid internet research also supplies an online integration contract; I treated reading that contract and downloading libraries as implementation, with no source research.\\\", \\\"Making one polished experience cover solo play, cooperative networking, controller, mouse, touch, kiosk replay and a single-file package.\\\", \\\"Specify whether standalone multiplayer should require cross-device discovery or allow manual WebRTC invitation codes.\\\"],\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"The House of Creaks\\\",\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"A small flame. A very bad address.\\\",\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Explore a matchlit, four-floor mansion, recover a shattered urn, and escape its uninvited guests. Carry one object at a time and brave the dark alone or with up to three friends.\\\",\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Horror\\\",\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Haunted House (1982)\\\",\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"WASD / left stick move; Space / R2 match; E / Cross interact; Q / Circle drop; Shift / L1 hush; F / Square ward; Tab / Triangle map; Esc / Options pause; mouse aim and use; touch drag and tap.\\\",\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"horror\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"exploration\\\", \\\"isometric\\\", \\\"retro\\\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 build.py\nnode --check main.mjs\nnode --check core.mjs\nnode --input-type=module -e \\\"import {HouseGame} from './core.mjs'; await HouseGame.init(); let g=new HouseGame(); g.reset([{id:0}]); g.update(.016,{0:{x:1}}); console.log(JSON.stringify({player:g.player(),colliders:g.world.colliders.len()}));g.dispose()\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"Built The-House-of-Creaks-Haunted-House-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-191354.html\nusing deprecated parameters for the initialization function; pass a single object instead\n{\"player\":{\"id\":0,\"name\":\"Guest\",\"color\":\"#79ddc8\",\"f\":0,\"x\":-0.47960000038146977,\"z\":5.2,\"angle\":1.5707963267948966,\"health\":5,\"match\":0,\"matches\":16,\"carry\":null,\"invuln\":1.984,\"cooldown\":0,\"stairCD\":0,\"hush\":false,\"moving\":true,\"rested\":[],\"connected\":true,\"actions\":{\"interact\":false,\"match\":false,\"drop\":false,\"pulse\":false},\"seen\":[],\"score\":5},\"colliders\":29}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tests/smoke.py <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom http.server import ThreadingHTTPServer, SimpleHTTPRequestHandler\nfrom functools import partial\nimport threading, json\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nroot=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nclass Quiet(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self,*args): pass\nserver=ThreadingHTTPServer(('127.0.0.1',0),partial(Quiet,directory=str(root)))\nthreading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever,daemon=True).start()\nurl=f'http://127.0.0.1:{server.server_port}/{root.name if False else Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1].name}.html'\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader','--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\n    page=browser.new_page(viewport={'width':1600,'height':1000},device_scale_factor=1)\n    errors=[]\n    page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)))\n    page.on('console',lambda m: errors.append(m.text) if m.type=='error' else None)\n    page.goto(url,wait_until='load')\n    try:page.wait_for_function('window.__creaks?.ready',timeout=90000)\n    except Exception:pass\n    print(json.dumps({'url':url,'title':page.title(),'errors':errors,'loading':page.locator('#loadMessage').inner_text(),'state':page.evaluate('window.__creaks?.state()')},indent=2))\n    page.screenshot(path=str(Path(__file__).parent/'title.png'))\n    browser.close()\nserver.shutdown()\nEOF\n/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python tests/smoke.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tests/core.test.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport {HouseGame,DEFAULTS,roomAt} from '../core.mjs';\nconst failures=[];let count=0;\nconst warning=console.warn;console.warn=()=>{};await HouseGame.init();console.warn=warning;\nfunction test(name,fn){count++;try{fn()}catch(e){failures.push(name+': '+e.message)}}\nconst games=[];function make(){const g=new HouseGame();g.reset([{id:0,name:'Test'}]);games.push(g);return g}\nfunction walk(g,x,z){const p=g.player(),path=g.pathTo(p,x,z);assert.ok(path.length||Math.hypot(p.x-x,p.z-z)<.6,'no navigable path');for(const q of path){let n=0;while(Math.hypot(q.x-p.x,q.z-p.z)>.13&&n++<100){const dx=q.x-p.x,dz=q.z-p.z,d=Math.hypot(dx,dz);g.update(1/60,{0:{x:dx/d,z:dz/d}})}assert.ok(n<100,\"'`stuck near ${p.x.toFixed(1)},${p.z.toFixed(1)} towards ${q.x},${q.z}`)}assert.ok(Math.hypot(p.x-x,p.z-z)<.9,'\"'wrong destination')}\nfunction act(g){g.player().stairCD=0;return g.interact(g.player())}\ntest('Four floors, three fragments, one key and one ward',()=>{const g=make();assert.equal(g.items.length,5);assert.equal(g.enemies.length,13);assert.equal(g.visited.length,4)});\ntest('Rapier blocks solid walls',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,-6,-8);for(let i=0;i<90;i++)g.update(1/60,{0:{x:1}});assert.ok(p.x<-5.3,\"'`crossed wall: ${p.x}`)});\ntest('\"'Rapier allows door crossings',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.god=true;g.teleport(p,-6,-5);for(let i=0;i<70;i++)g.update(1/60,{0:{x:1}});assert.ok(p.x>-2,'door blocked')});\ntest('Match consumes one and expires',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();assert.ok(g.ignite(p));assert.equal(p.matches,15);assert.equal(p.match,12);for(let i=0;i<721;i++)g.update(1/60);assert.equal(p.match,0)});\ntest('Holding match input does not consume repeatedly',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();for(let i=0;i<60;i++)g.update(1/60,{0:{match:true}});assert.equal(p.matches,15)});\ntest('No matches gives a usable hint',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.matches=0;assert.equal(g.ignite(p),false);assert.match(g.events.at(-1).text,/candle/)});\ntest('Taking a second item swaps a single held object',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,10,-6.6);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'key');const ward=g.items.find(i=>i.id==='ward');ward.f=0;ward.x=10.6;ward.z=-6.6;g.teleport(p,10.6,-6.6);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'ward');assert.equal(g.items.find(i=>i.id==='key').holder,null)});\ntest('The brass lock consumes the key and stays open',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,-12,-7,1);assert.equal(act(g),false);assert.equal(p.f,1);const key=g.items.find(i=>i.id==='key');key.holder=0;p.carry='key';assert.ok(act(g));assert.equal(p.f,2);assert.equal(g.unlocked,true);assert.equal(p.carry,null);assert.equal(key.banked,true)});\ntest('Safe candles refill and heal only once per floor',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,0,5);p.matches=0;p.health=2;act(g);assert.equal(p.matches,18);assert.equal(p.health,3);p.health=2;act(g);assert.equal(p.health,2)});\ntest('Unprotected wind extinguishes a match',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,10,5);p.match=8;g.time=DEFAULTS.windInterval-4-.01;g.update(.02,{0:{}});assert.equal(g.wind,1);assert.equal(p.match,0)});\ntest('Hush protects immediately on the gust frame',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,10,5);p.match=8;g.time=DEFAULTS.windInterval-4-.01;g.update(.02,{0:{hush:true}});assert.ok(p.match>7)});\ntest('Scepter pulses stun nearby enemies and enforce cooldown',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.carry='ward';g.items.find(i=>i.id==='ward').holder=0;const e=g.enemies[0];e.x=p.x+2;e.z=p.z;assert.ok(g.pulse(p));assert.equal(e.stun,6);assert.equal(g.pulse(p),false)});\ntest('Bats snuff a lit match before harming nerves',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.invuln=0;p.match=6;assert.ok(g.hit(p,{type:'bat'}));assert.equal(p.match,0);assert.equal(p.health,5)});\ntest('A hit drops the held item and gives invulnerability',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.invuln=0;p.carry='key';g.items.find(i=>i.id==='key').holder=0;g.hit(p,{type:'ghost'});assert.equal(p.health,4);assert.equal(p.carry,null);g.hit(p,{type:'ghost'});assert.equal(p.health,4)});\ntest('A zero-nerve solo player reaches loss',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.health=1;p.invuln=0;g.hit(p,{type:'ghost'});assert.equal(g.status,'lost');assert.equal(g.finished,true)});\ntest('Co-op companions keep the night alive',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.addPlayer({id:1,name:'Friend'});p.health=1;p.invuln=0;g.hit(p,{type:'ghost'});assert.equal(g.status,'playing');assert.equal(p.health,3);assert.equal(p.f,0)});\ntest('Snapshots restore all progression and physical bodies',()=>{const a=make(),b=make();a.addPlayer({id:1});a.unlocked=true;a.teleport(a.player(),11,3,2);a.banked=['shard0'];a.items[2].banked=true;assert.ok(b.apply(a.snapshot()));assert.equal(b.players.length,2);assert.equal(b.player().f,2);assert.equal(b.unlocked,true);assert.equal(b.bodies.size,2);assert.equal(b.banked[0],'shard0')});\ntest('Disconnect drops carried items',()=>{const g=make();g.addPlayer({id:1});const p=g.players[1];p.carry='key';g.items[0].holder=1;g.removePlayer(1);assert.equal(g.items[0].holder,null);assert.equal(g.players.length,1)});\ntest('Complete physical playthrough recovers all fragments and escapes',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.god=true;walk(g,10,-6.6);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'key');walk(g,12,7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,1);walk(g,-12,-7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,2);assert.ok(g.unlocked);walk(g,-10,5.8);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'shard1');walk(g,-12,-7);act(g);walk(g,12,7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,0);walk(g,0,6.2);act(g);assert.ok(g.banked.includes('shard1'));walk(g,12,7);act(g);walk(g,0,-5.8);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'shard0');walk(g,12,7);act(g);walk(g,0,6.2);act(g);assert.equal(g.banked.length,2);walk(g,12,7);act(g);walk(g,-12,-7);act(g);walk(g,12,7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,3);walk(g,10,-6.2);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'shard2');walk(g,12,7);act(g);walk(g,-12,-7);act(g);walk(g,12,7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,0);walk(g,0,6.2);act(g);assert.equal(g.banked.length,3);walk(g,0,9);act(g);assert.equal(g.status,'won');assert.ok(g.stairsUsed>=12);assert.equal(g.recovered,3)});\nfor(const g of games)g.dispose();process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({count,failures}));\nEOF\nnode tests/core.test.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tests/core.test.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport {HouseGame,DEFAULTS,roomAt} from '../core.mjs';\nconst failures=[];let count=0;\nconst warning=console.warn;console.warn=()=>{};await HouseGame.init();console.warn=warning;\nfunction test(name,fn){count++;try{fn()}catch(e){failures.push(name+': '+e.message)}}\nconst games=[];function make(){const g=new HouseGame();g.reset([{id:0,name:'Test'}]);games.push(g);return g}\nfunction walk(g,x,z){const p=g.player(),path=g.pathTo(p,x,z);assert.ok(path.length||Math.hypot(p.x-x,p.z-z)<.6,'no navigable path');for(const q of path){let n=0;while(Math.hypot(q.x-p.x,q.z-p.z)>.13&&n++<100){const dx=q.x-p.x,dz=q.z-p.z,d=Math.hypot(dx,dz);g.update(1/60,{0:{x:dx/d,z:dz/d}})}assert.ok(n<100,\"'`stuck near ${p.x.toFixed(1)},${p.z.toFixed(1)} towards ${q.x},${q.z}`)}assert.ok(Math.hypot(p.x-x,p.z-z)<.9,'\"'wrong destination')}\nfunction act(g){g.player().stairCD=0;return g.interact(g.player())}\ntest('Four floors, three fragments, one key and one ward',()=>{const g=make();assert.equal(g.items.length,5);assert.equal(g.enemies.length,13);assert.equal(g.visited.length,4)});\ntest('Rapier blocks solid walls',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,-6,-8);for(let i=0;i<90;i++)g.update(1/60,{0:{x:1}});assert.ok(p.x<-5.3,\"'`crossed wall: ${p.x}`)});\ntest('\"'Rapier allows door crossings',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.god=true;g.teleport(p,-6,-5);for(let i=0;i<70;i++)g.update(1/60,{0:{x:1}});assert.ok(p.x>-2,'door blocked')});\ntest('Match consumes one and expires',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();assert.ok(g.ignite(p));assert.equal(p.matches,15);assert.equal(p.match,12);for(let i=0;i<721;i++)g.update(1/60);assert.equal(p.match,0)});\ntest('Holding match input does not consume repeatedly',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();for(let i=0;i<60;i++)g.update(1/60,{0:{match:true}});assert.equal(p.matches,15)});\ntest('No matches gives a usable hint',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.matches=0;assert.equal(g.ignite(p),false);assert.match(g.events.at(-1).text,/candle/)});\ntest('Taking a second item swaps a single held object',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,10,-6.6);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'key');const ward=g.items.find(i=>i.id==='ward');ward.f=0;ward.x=10.6;ward.z=-6.6;g.teleport(p,10.6,-6.6);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'ward');assert.equal(g.items.find(i=>i.id==='key').holder,null)});\ntest('The brass lock consumes the key and stays open',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,-12,-7,1);assert.equal(act(g),false);assert.equal(p.f,1);const key=g.items.find(i=>i.id==='key');key.holder=0;p.carry='key';assert.ok(act(g));assert.equal(p.f,2);assert.equal(g.unlocked,true);assert.equal(p.carry,null);assert.equal(key.banked,true)});\ntest('Safe candles refill and heal only once per floor',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,0,5);p.matches=0;p.health=2;act(g);assert.equal(p.matches,18);assert.equal(p.health,3);p.health=2;act(g);assert.equal(p.health,2)});\ntest('Unprotected wind extinguishes a match',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,10,5);p.match=8;g.time=DEFAULTS.windInterval-4-.01;g.update(.02,{0:{}});assert.equal(g.wind,1);assert.equal(p.match,0)});\ntest('Hush protects immediately on the gust frame',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.teleport(p,10,5);p.match=8;g.time=DEFAULTS.windInterval-4-.01;g.update(.02,{0:{hush:true}});assert.ok(p.match>7)});\ntest('Scepter pulses stun nearby enemies and enforce cooldown',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.carry='ward';g.items.find(i=>i.id==='ward').holder=0;const e=g.enemies[0];e.x=p.x+2;e.z=p.z;assert.ok(g.pulse(p));assert.equal(e.stun,6);assert.equal(g.pulse(p),false)});\ntest('Bats snuff a lit match before harming nerves',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.invuln=0;p.match=6;assert.ok(g.hit(p,{type:'bat'}));assert.equal(p.match,0);assert.equal(p.health,5)});\ntest('A hit drops the held item and gives invulnerability',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.invuln=0;p.carry='key';g.items.find(i=>i.id==='key').holder=0;g.hit(p,{type:'ghost'});assert.equal(p.health,4);assert.equal(p.carry,null);g.hit(p,{type:'ghost'});assert.equal(p.health,4)});\ntest('A zero-nerve solo player reaches loss',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();p.health=1;p.invuln=0;g.hit(p,{type:'ghost'});assert.equal(g.status,'lost');assert.equal(g.finished,true)});\ntest('Co-op companions keep the night alive',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.addPlayer({id:1,name:'Friend'});p.health=1;p.invuln=0;g.hit(p,{type:'ghost'});assert.equal(g.status,'playing');assert.equal(p.health,3);assert.equal(p.f,0)});\ntest('Snapshots restore all progression and physical bodies',()=>{const a=make(),b=make();a.addPlayer({id:1});a.unlocked=true;a.teleport(a.player(),11,3,2);a.banked=['shard0'];a.items[2].banked=true;assert.ok(b.apply(a.snapshot()));assert.equal(b.players.length,2);assert.equal(b.player().f,2);assert.equal(b.unlocked,true);assert.equal(b.bodies.size,2);assert.equal(b.banked[0],'shard0')});\ntest('Disconnect drops carried items',()=>{const g=make();g.addPlayer({id:1});const p=g.players[1];p.carry='key';g.items[0].holder=1;g.removePlayer(1);assert.equal(g.items[0].holder,null);assert.equal(g.players.length,1)});\ntest('Complete physical playthrough recovers all fragments and escapes',()=>{const g=make(),p=g.player();g.god=true;walk(g,10,-6.6);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'key');walk(g,12,7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,1);walk(g,-12,-7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,2);assert.ok(g.unlocked);walk(g,-10,5.8);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'shard1');walk(g,-12,-7);act(g);walk(g,12,7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,0);walk(g,0,6.2);act(g);assert.ok(g.banked.includes('shard1'));walk(g,12,7);act(g);walk(g,0,-5.8);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'shard0');walk(g,12,7);act(g);walk(g,0,6.2);act(g);assert.equal(g.banked.length,2);walk(g,12,7);act(g);walk(g,-12,-7);act(g);walk(g,12,7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,3);walk(g,10,-6.2);act(g);assert.equal(p.carry,'shard2');walk(g,12,7);act(g);walk(g,-12,-7);act(g);walk(g,12,7);act(g);assert.equal(p.f,0);walk(g,0,6.2);act(g);assert.equal(g.banked.length,3);walk(g,0,9);act(g);assert.equal(g.status,'won');assert.ok(g.stairsUsed>=12);assert.equal(g.recovered,3)});\nfor(const g of games)g.dispose();process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({count,failures}));\nEOF\nnode tests/core.test.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"{\"count\":19,\"failures\":[\"Four floors, three fragments, one key and one ward: Expected values to be strictly equal:\\n\\n12 !== 13\\n\",\"Hush protects immediately on the gust frame: The expression evaluated to a falsy value:\\n\\n  assert.ok(p.match>7)\\n\",\"Complete physical playthrough recovers all fragments and escapes: The expression evaluated to a falsy value:\\n\\n  assert.ok(g.banked.includes('shard1'))\\n\"]}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"The first tests found two behaviour issues: Hush was applied a frame too late when a gust began, and returning a fragment near the foyer candle could select “rest” instead of the urn plinth. I’m fixing both. The same suite checks doors, walls, swapping, enemy hits, co-op recovery, and the full collection-and-escape route.\n"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tests/smoke.py <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom http.server import ThreadingHTTPServer, SimpleHTTPRequestHandler\nfrom functools import partial\nimport threading, json\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nroot=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nclass Quiet(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self,*args): pass\nserver=ThreadingHTTPServer(('127.0.0.1',0),partial(Quiet,directory=str(root)))\nthreading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever,daemon=True).start()\nurl=f'http://127.0.0.1:{server.server_port}/{root.name if False else Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1].name}.html'\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader','--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\n    page=browser.new_page(viewport={'width':1600,'height':1000},device_scale_factor=1)\n    errors=[]\n    page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)))\n    page.on('console',lambda m: errors.append(m.text) if m.type=='error' else None)\n    page.goto(url,wait_until='load')\n    try:page.wait_for_function('window.__creaks?.ready',timeout=90000)\n    except Exception:pass\n    print(json.dumps({'url':url,'title':page.title(),'errors':errors,'loading':page.locator('#loadMessage').inner_text(),'state':page.evaluate('window.__creaks?.state()')},indent=2))\n    page.screenshot(path=str(Path(__file__).parent/'title.png'))\n    browser.close()\nserver.shutdown()\nEOF\n/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python tests/smoke.py\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"url\": \"http://127.0.0.1:45715/The-House-of-Creaks-Haunted-House-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-191354.html\",\n  \"title\": \"The House of Creaks\",\n  \"errors\": [\n    \"Identifier 'clamp' has already been declared\"\n  ],\n  \"loading\": \"Waking the house\\u2026\",\n  \"state\": null\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
