{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"agent_message","text":"Shared-world movement and fragment syncing work, but repeated headless WebGPU contexts remain unreliable on this machine. I’ll use fresh WebGPU processes for the single-player, input, and file-deployment checks, and the same renderer’s WebGL2 backend for the multi-page transport and Hub protocol tests. I’ll record that testing limit in the credits.\n"}}
