{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_108","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('metadata.json');j=json.loads(p.read_text());j['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless tests allowed: scripted full physical playthrough, mechanics assertions, browser state, virtual standard gamepad, real emulated touch events, Web Audio analyser, file deployment, two-page co-op and official AI Hub harness; screenshots for visual composition. Chromium WebGPU is used for solo/input/file checks, Chromium WebGL2 for direct WebRTC, and WebKit WebGL2 for same-browser rooms and Hub checks. Physical controller, real mobile hardware and cross-network NAT compatibility: unknown.'\nj['testingFeedback']=['8 game issues found and corrected: two timing/interaction faults, two packaging faults, three visual proportion/framing faults, and one Hub startup-order fault. Test-script mistakes and browser/environment restrictions were tracked separately.','3 startup blockers: a duplicate bundled identifier, the wrong Rapier CDN module filename, and graphics initialization delaying the Hub welcome handshake.','The official AI Hub conformance harness: it caught the startup ordering bug and checks time-up, departures, simulated network loss and server-only hosts.','Headless WebGPU screenshots were least useful because capture was corrupted on this machine. I used state checks and the WebGL2 backend for visual inspection.']\nj['engineFeedback']=['Three.js TSL gave all procedural objects a consistent cel palette, and AnimationMixer made reusable creature clips straightforward.','Yes. I initially used an obsolete Rapier module filename and let graphics startup delay the Hub handshake. Headless WebGPU contexts required isolated browser runs; direct WebRTC was verified in Chromium after WebKit did not connect.','The authoritative room, inventory, enemy, light and cooperative simulation, plus input-aware menus, procedural models and synthesized audio.','Coordinating asynchronous startup, fixed-step Rapier movement, native animation and replicated state in one HTML deliverable.','none','Add a first-party controller focus and navigation layer, including scrollable overlays.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(j,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nnpm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts > tests/npm-lock-feedback.txt 2>&1\ncat tests/progress.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_108","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('metadata.json');j=json.loads(p.read_text());j['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless tests allowed: scripted full physical playthrough, mechanics assertions, browser state, virtual standard gamepad, real emulated touch events, Web Audio analyser, file deployment, two-page co-op and official AI Hub harness; screenshots for visual composition. Chromium WebGPU is used for solo/input/file checks, Chromium WebGL2 for direct WebRTC, and WebKit WebGL2 for same-browser rooms and Hub checks. Physical controller, real mobile hardware and cross-network NAT compatibility: unknown.'\nj['testingFeedback']=['8 game issues found and corrected: two timing/interaction faults, two packaging faults, three visual proportion/framing faults, and one Hub startup-order fault. Test-script mistakes and browser/environment restrictions were tracked separately.','3 startup blockers: a duplicate bundled identifier, the wrong Rapier CDN module filename, and graphics initialization delaying the Hub welcome handshake.','The official AI Hub conformance harness: it caught the startup ordering bug and checks time-up, departures, simulated network loss and server-only hosts.','Headless WebGPU screenshots were least useful because capture was corrupted on this machine. I used state checks and the WebGL2 backend for visual inspection.']\nj['engineFeedback']=['Three.js TSL gave all procedural objects a consistent cel palette, and AnimationMixer made reusable creature clips straightforward.','Yes. I initially used an obsolete Rapier module filename and let graphics startup delay the Hub handshake. Headless WebGPU contexts required isolated browser runs; direct WebRTC was verified in Chromium after WebKit did not connect.','The authoritative room, inventory, enemy, light and cooperative simulation, plus input-aware menus, procedural models and synthesized audio.','Coordinating asynchronous startup, fixed-step Rapier movement, native animation and replicated state in one HTML deliverable.','none','Add a first-party controller focus and navigation layer, including scrollable overlays.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(j,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nnpm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts > tests/npm-lock-feedback.txt 2>&1\ncat tests/progress.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"check\": 49, \"stage\": \"Math.abs(__creaks.state().players[1].z-5.2)>.2\"}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('main.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace('status: net.status,','status: net.status,\\\\n                receivedInputs: net.inputs,\\\\n                heldKeys: [...keys],');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nbiome check --write main.mjs > tests/biome-feedback.txt 2>&1\npython3 build.py\ncat > tests/rtc-probe.py <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom http.server import ThreadingHTTPServer,SimpleHTTPRequestHandler\nfrom functools import partial\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse,unquote\nimport threading,json\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nD=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];R=D.parent\nclass Quiet(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n def log_message(self,*args):pass\ns=ThreadingHTTPServer(('127.0.0.1',0),partial(Quiet,directory=str(R)));threading.Thread(target=s.serve_forever,daemon=True).start()\ndef dep(route):\n path=unquote(urlparse(route.request.url).path)\n if '/three@0.180.0/build/' in path:f=D/'node_modules/three/build'/path.split('/')[-1]\n elif '/@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3/' in path:f=D/'node_modules/@dimforge/rapier3d-compat'/path.split('/')[-1]\n else:route.continue_();return\n route.fulfill(path=str(f),content_type='text/javascript',headers={'Access-Control-Allow-Origin':'*'})\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n b=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--use-angle=swiftshader','--enable-unsafe-swiftshader','--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']);c=b.new_context(viewport={'width':640,'height':480});c.route('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/**',dep)\n pages=[]\n for _ in range(2):\n  page=c.new_page();page.goto(f'http://127.0.0.1:{s.server_port}/{D.name}.html?renderer=webgl');page.wait_for_function('window.__creaks?.ready');pages.append(page)\n host,guest=pages\n host.evaluate('__creaks.createOffer()');offer=host.evaluate('__creaks.offer()');guest.evaluate('(v)=>__creaks.acceptOffer(v)',offer);answer=guest.evaluate('__creaks.answer()');host.evaluate('(v)=>__creaks.acceptAnswer(v)',answer);guest.wait_for_function('__creaks.state().net.me===1');host.evaluate('__creaks.start()');guest.wait_for_function('__creaks.state().screen===\\\"game\\\"');guest.keyboard.down('KeyS');guest.wait_for_timeout(2500)\n for name,page in zip(['host','guest'],pages):\n  print(json.dumps({'name':name,'state':page.evaluate('(()=>{const s=__creaks.state();return {time:s.time,screen:s.screen,paused:s.paused,players:s.players,net:s.net,focus:document.activeElement.outerHTML.slice(0,200)}})()')},indent=2),flush=True)\n guest.keyboard.up('KeyS');b.close()\ns.shutdown()\nEOF\n/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python tests/rtc-probe.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
